se"],["अध्यवसीयते प्रकाशते च","by whom they are understood and illumined"],["परं ब्रह्म परमात्मा","the Supreme Brahman, the Supreme Self"],["आश्रयः कथ्यते","is called the support"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":8,"end":8,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["आध्यात्मिकः पुरुषः","the individual self"],["चक्षुरादि-करणाभिमानी द्रष्टा जीवः","the living seer identified with the eye and other faculties"],["अधिदैविकः चक्षुराद्यधिष्ठाता सूर्यादिः","the presiding deity, such as the sun"],["आधिभौतिकः चक्षुर्गोलकादिः","the physical eye and the like"],["दृश्यो देहः पुरुषस्य उपाधिः","the visible body is an adjunct of the person"],["विच्छेदः भेदः विभागः","viccheda means distinction or division"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":9,"end":9,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["एकम् एकतराभावः","one means the absence of any one [of the three]"],["अन्योन्यसापेक्षसिद्धित्वेन","because each is established in dependence on the others"],["दृश्यं विना करणं न सिध्यति","without an object, the sense faculty is not established"],["द्रष्टा न सिध्यति","nor is the seer"],["तदधिष्ठाता सूर्यादिः","nor the presiding deity, such as the sun"],["त्रितयं यो वेद","the one who knows the three"],["स्वाश्रयः अनन्याश्रयः","self-dependent, dependent on no other"],["अन्येषाम् आश्रयः","the support of the others"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":10,"end":10,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["पुरुषः वैराजः","the Virāṭ Puruṣa"],["अण्डं विनिर्भिद्य","having split the cosmic egg"],["पृथक् कृत्य विनिर्गतः","having separated it, he came forth"],["अयनं स्थानम्","ayana means place"],["शुचिः स्वयम्","pure himself"],["शुचीः अपः अस्राक्षीत्","he created the pure waters"]],"note":"The source spells 