er of mind"],["बलं देहशक्तिः","bala is bodily strength"],["सूक्ष्माद् रूपात् प्राणः सूत्राख्यः","from the subtle form comes prāṇa, called the thread"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":16,"end":16,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["प्राणाः इन्द्रियाणि","the prāṇas are the senses"],["यं प्राणन्तम् अनु","following him as he acts"],["अपानन्तम् अनु","following him as he withdraws"],["राजानम् अनु भृत्याः इव","like servants following their king"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":17,"end":17,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["क्षिपता चालयता","by one who casts and moves"],["क्षुत्तृडादिकम्","hunger, thirst, and the like"],["प्रभोः","of the Lord"],["जक्षतः भक्षयितुम् इच्छतः","of one who wishes to eat"],["निरभिद्यत विभक्तम् अभूत्","it was divided and became distinct"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":18,"end":18,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["तालु अधिष्ठानम्","the palate is the seat"],["जिह्वेन्द्रियम्","the tongue is the sense"],["नाना-रसः विषयः","the various tastes are its objects"],["वरुणः देवता","Varuṇa is the presiding deity"],["अधिष्ठानम् इन्द्रियम् देवता विषयः","seat, sense, deity, and object"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":19,"end":20,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["विवक्षोः वक्तुम् इच्छोः","of one who desires to speak"],["मुखतः","from the mouth"],["वह्निः देवता","fire is the presiding deity"],["वाक् इन्द्रियम्","speech is the sense"],["व्याहृतं भाषणम्","utterance is speaking"],["नासिकायां वायुः देवता","in the nostrils, air is the presiding deity"],["गन्धं वहति","it carries scent"],["घ्राण इन्द्रियम्","smell is the sense"],["जिघृक्षतः गन्धं ग्रहीतुम् इच्छतः","of one who wishes to grasp a scent"]],"note":"The source groups 2.10.19–20 in one Śrīdhara block; both verses are covered by this WFW record."},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":21,"end":21,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["निरालोकम् प्रकाशशून्यम्","without light, devoid of illumination"],["आत्मानं देहं च दिदृक्षतः","of one wishing to see himself, the body"],["अक्षिणी स्थानम्","the eyes are the seat"],["ज्योतिः आदित्यः देवता","light, the sun, is the presiding deity"],["चक्षुः इन्द्रियम्","sight is the sense"],["रूपं विषयः","form is the object"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":22,"end":22,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["ऋषिभिः वेदैः बोध्यमानस्य","of the one made known by sages and the Vedas"],["आत्मनः प्रबोधनम्","the awakening of the self"],["ग्रहीतुम् इच्छतः","of one wishing to grasp"],["शब्दस्य ग्रहणम्","the apprehension of sound"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":23,"end":23,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["मृदुत्वं काठिन्यं लघुत्वं गुरुत्वं च","softness, hardness, lightness, and heaviness"],["उष्णत्वम् ईषदुष्णत्वं शीतता च","heat, slight warmth, and cold"],["त्वक् इन्द्रियम्","the skin is the sense"],["रोमाणि महीरुहाश्च देवताः","the hairs and plants are presiding powers"],["स्पर्शः गुणः","touch is the quality perceived"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":24,"end":24,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["रुरुहतुः निर्भिन्नौ","the two [hands] emerged"],["बलम् इन्द्रियम्","strength is the sense"],["इन्द्रः देवता","Indra is the presiding deity"],["आदानं कर्म","taking hold is the action"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":25,"end":25,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["अभिकामिकाम् अभीष्टां हिताम्","desired, cherished, beneficial"],["पद्भ्यां सह यज्ञः विष्णुः","with the feet, sacrifice itself is Viṣṇu"],["गत्याख्या कर्मशक्तिः इन्द्रियम्","locomotion is the active power, the sense"],["हव्यं यज्ञार्थं द्रव्यम्","an oblation is an object offered in sacrifice"],["विषयः","the object [of movement]"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":26,"end":26,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["प्रजा अपत्यम्","praja means offspring"],["आनन्दः रतिः अमृतं स्वर्गादि","pleasure, sexual delight, immortality, and heaven"],["शिश्नः अधिष्ठानम्","the generative organ is the seat"],["उपस्थम् इन्द्रियम्","the organ of generation is the sense"],["प्रजापतिः देवता","Prajāpati is the presiding deity"],["प्रियं सुखम्","the pleasure sought is happiness"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":27,"end":27,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["धातुमलम्","the waste of the bodily tissues"],["भुक्तान्नादीनाम् असारांशम्","the rejected portion of food and the like"],["त्यक्तुम् इच्छोः","of one wishing to expel"],["गुद-पायु-मित्रोत्सर्गाः","the anus, rectum, and excretion"],["अधिष्ठान-इन्द्रिय-देवता-विषयाः","the seat, sense, deity, and object"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":28,"end":28,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["पुर्याः देहात्","from the city, the body"],["देहान्तराणि आसिसृप्सोः","of one wishing to go to other bodies"],["नाभिद्वारम्","the navel passage"],["अपानतः अपगच्छतः","as the life air departs"],["पृथक्त्वं मरणम्","separation is death"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":29,"end":29,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["अन्नपानानाम् आदित्सोः","of one wishing to take in food and drink"],["कुक्षिः अन्त्राणि नाड्यश्च","the abdomen, intestines, and channels"],["अन्नसंग्रहे करणम्","the intestines are the instrument for holding food"],["नाड्यः पानं ग्रहे","the channels receive liquids"],["नद्यः समुद्राश्च देवताः","rivers and oceans are their deities"],["तुष्टिः उदरभरणम्","contentment is filling the belly"],["पुष्टिः रसपरिणामतः स्थौल्यम्","nourishment is fullness from the transformation of food"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":30,"end":30,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["निदिध्यासोः नितरां चिन्तयितुम् इच्छोः","of one who wishes to contemplate deeply"],["कामः अभिलाषः","kāma means desire"],["हृदय-मनः-चन्द्र-संकल्पाः","the heart, mind, and moon preside over resolve"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":31,"end":31,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["त्वक् स्थूलम्","skin is gross"],["चर्म तदुपरि स्थितं सूक्ष्मम्","the hide above it is subtle"],["त्वगादयः अस्थ्यन्ताः सप्त धातवः","the seven constituents, from skin through bone"],["भूम्य्-अप्-तेजोमयाः","composed of earth, water, and fire"],["वाय्वाकाशयोः संवर्धकत्वाभावात्","because air and ether do not nourish them"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":32,"end":32,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["गुणात्मकानि गुणेषु शब्दादिषु","made of qualities, directed toward sound and the other objects"],["विषयाभिमुखस्वभावानि","whose nature faces sense objects"],["अहंकारकल्पितशोभनस्वभावाः","appearing attractive by the construction of ego"],["मनः सर्वविकाराणाम् आत्मा","the mind is the source of all modifications"],["संकल्पविकल्पमात्रम्","only forming intentions and doubts"],["बुद्धिः तथाभूतार्थविज्ञानरूपिणी","intellect is awareness of things as they appear"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":33,"end":33,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["उपसंहरति","he summarizes"],["प्रकृत्या सह अष्टभिः","together with prakṛti and the eight [principles]"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":34,"end":34,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["स्थूलम् उक्त्वा","having spoken of the gross"],["सूक्ष्मं समष्टि-लिङ्ग-शरीरम्","the subtle, aggregate liṅga body"],["अतीन्द्रियम् अव्यक्तम्","beyond the senses, unmanifest"],["अनादि-मध्य-निधनम्","without beginning, middle, or end"],["नित्यं सदैक-रूपम्","eternal and always of one nature"],["वाक् च मनः च तस्मात् परम्","beyond speech and mind"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":35,"end":35,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["उपासनार्थम् आरोपितं रूपद्वयम्","the two forms superimposed for worship"],["न गृह्णन्ति न अङ्गीकुर्वन्ति","they do not accept as ultimate"],["मायासृष्टे","because they are created by māyā"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":36,"end":36,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["ब्रह्मरूपधृक् सन्","assuming the form of Brahmā"],["नामानि वाच्यतया","names as words"],["रूपाणि वाच्यतया","forms as their referents"],["क्रियाः धत्ते सृजति","he assumes the acts, he creates"],["मायया सकर्मा सव्यापारः","active and engaged through māyā"],["वस्तुतः अकर्मकः","in reality inactive"]],"note":"The source has the broken spelling “नमानि”; the WFW restores the clear contextual form “नामानि”."},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":37,"end":39,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["प्रजापतीन् मरीचिप्रमुखान्","the Prajāpatis, headed by Marīci"],["नामानि तत्-तद्-वाच्यानि","names and the things denoted by them"],["रूपाणि तत्-तत्-कर्माणि","forms and their respective functions"],["द्विविधाः स्थावर-जङ्गम-रूपेण","two kinds: stationary and moving"],["चतुर्विधाः जरायुज-अण्डज-स्वेदज-उद्भिज्जाः","four kinds: womb-born, egg-born, moisture-born, and sprout-born"],["जल-स्थल-नभांसि ओकांसि","their homes in water, on land, and in the sky"]],"note":"The Śrīdhara commentary groups 2.10.37–39 in one block; WFW preserves the range."},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":40,"end":41,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["कुशलाः उत्तमाः","the good are superior"],["अकुशलाः नीचाः","the bad are inferior"],["मिश्राः मध्यमाः","the mixed are intermediate"],["कर्मणां पुण्य-पाप-मिश्राणाम्","of actions mixed with merit and sin"],["फलानि गतयः","the results are destinations"],["सत्त्वादयः तिस्रः गतयः","sattva and the other two are the three courses"],["अन्याभ्यां गुणाभ्यां स्वभावः अनुविध्यते","one’s nature is affected by the other two qualities"]],"note":"The source groups 2.10.40–41 in one Śrīdhara block; WFW preserves the range."},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":42,"end":42,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["ब्रह्मरूपेण स्रष्टृत्वम्","creation in the form of Brahmā"],["विष्णुरूपेण पालकत्वम्","protection in the form of Viṣṇu"],["तिर्यगाद्यवतारैः","through incarnations such as animals"],["विश्वं स्थापयन् पालयन्","establishing and protecting the universe"],["धर्मरूपेण पुष्णाति","he nourishes it as dharma"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":43,"end":43,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["रुद्ररूपेण","in the form of Rudra"],["संहर्तृत्वम्","the act of dissolution"],["आत्मनः सकाशात्","from himself"],["सृष्टं तत् सन्नियच्छति संहरति","he withdraws and dissolves what was created"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":44,"end":44,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["कर्तृत्वादि-अपवादेन","by denying agency and the rest"],["दशमस्य शुद्धिम्","the purity of the tenth topic"],["इत्थंभावेन स्रष्टृत्वादिरूपेण","in this manner, as the creator and so on"],["सूरयः","the sages"],["एवंरूपेण द्रष्टुं नार्हन्ति","cannot see him only in this form"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":45,"end":45,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["जन्मादौ कर्मणि","in the act of the world’s origin and the rest"],["परस्य ईश्वरस्य कर्तृत्वं नास्ति","the Supreme Lord has no agency"],["श्रुत्या तात्पर्येण न प्रतिपाद्यते","the Veda does not ultimately teach this as fact"],["कर्तृत्वप्रतिषेधार्थम्","for the purpose of denying agency"],["मायया आरोपितं प्रकाशितम्","projected and made manifest through māyā"],["निष्कलं निष्क्रियं शान्तम्","partless, inactive, peaceful"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":46,"end":46,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["ब्रह्मणः सम्बन्धी कल्पः","a kalpa belonging to Brahmā"],["महाकल्पः","a great kalpa"],["विकल्पः अवान्तरः","a vikalpa is an intermediate cycle"],["प्राकृताः महदादिसर्गाः","the primary creations beginning with mahat"],["वैकृताः स्थावर-विसर्गाः","the secondary creation of stationary beings"],["विधिः प्रकारः","vidhi means method"]],"note":"The source prints “विधिह्”; the WFW uses the standard form “विधिः”."},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":47,"end":47,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["वक्ष्यमाणं विस्तरम्","the detail to be explained"],["परिमाणं स्थूलं सूक्ष्मं च","the scale, gross and subtle"],["कल्पस्य लक्षणम्","the characteristic of the kalpa"],["अवान्तरकल्पं मन्वन्तरादिरूपम्","the intermediate cycles, such as Manvantaras"],["तृतीयस्कन्धे व्याख्यास्यामि","I will explain in the Third Canto"]]},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":48,"end":50,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["सृष्ट्यादिनिरूपणम्","the description of creation and the rest"],["श्रोतुकामः","wishing to hear"],["क्षत्ता विदुरः","Kṣattā is Vidura"],["भुवः सम्बन्धीनि तीर्थानि","the sacred places associated with the earth"],["मैत्रेयस्य संवादः","the dialogue with Maitreya"],["अध्यात्मज्ञानसंश्रितः","connected with spiritual knowledge"],["पुनः आगतवान् तत्र च निमित्तम्","why he returned there"],["ब्रूहि","tell [me]"]],"note":"The Śrīdhara commentary groups 2.10.48–50 in one block; WFW preserves the range."},{"canto":2,"chapter":10,"start":51,"end":51,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/10_indriyAdy-utpattiH.md","source_blob_sha":"78979d596cb7e429e2c2200c40a4ba0e22b0a4a3","pairs":[["राज्ञा पृष्ट इति","‘asked by the king’"],["यद् यूयं पृच्छथ","what you are asking"],["पूर्वं राज्ञा कृताः प्रश्नाः","the questions previously asked by the king"],["सर्वं पुराणार्थम् अवोचन्","he explained the whole meaning of the Purāṇa"],["तद् अहं वोऽभिधास्यामि","that I shall explain to you"],["तथैव शृणुत","listen in the same way"]],"note":"The source has several broken spellings/joins (“अर्थह्”, “अभिधास्य् आमि”); the WFW normalizes them to “अर्थः” and “अभिधास्यामि”."}]}